   "notes": [
    "Capo 1, Em shapes (sounds in F minor). 92 BPM (measured 91.97), timed to your MP3: first downbeat 3.46 s after a sung pickup; bar lines checked against the bass (gate 9).",
    "Tutorial (Telugu Guitar Songs): “capo on the first fret … the chords are E minor, C major, A minor and D major … strumming pattern down up down down.”",
    "Strumming, as the tutor plays it (keep the hand moving in 16ths: down on the beat and the &, up on e and a): D . . . | D . d u | . u d . | D . d u. Accent beats 1, 2 and 4.",
    "MJ Music Notes writes the pattern as DDD-DU-DUDD-DU; it can't be placed on the beat grid without guessing, so it isn't used as a pattern.",
    "Shapes with capo 1: Em = Fm, Am = B♭m, D = E♭, G = A♭, C = D♭, Bm = Cm, A = B♭. Easy plays Bm as Bm7 (x20202).",
    "Pattern 1 (Easy): D D U D D from YouTube's Ask summary of your tutorial at 0:36 — down on 1, 2, up on the & of 2, down on 3 and 4, no up after 4. It replaces ChordZone's generic DU DU DU DU. The measured tutorial pattern (Hard) ends with a light up on the a of 4."
   ],
